udeck-plugin: third-party notices
=================================

udeck-plugin is uDeck's own, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE, beside
this file) with uDeck's NOTICE. Built, it is also made of the software below,
under the licences named. Which copy holds what:

  * the archive for macOS (universal) links the Swift runtime, Foundation and
    CryptoKit of macOS itself, which are not in it; of what follows it holds
    only swift-crypto's Crypto module (1), which on a Mac hands its work to
    CryptoKit;
  * the archives for Linux (static musl, x86_64 and aarch64) hold all of 1-10:
    the binary is static, so everything it runs is in the one file;
  * the container image holds the Linux binary, so 1-10, and Alpine Linux's
    packages besides — the programs the command starts, and what they need:
    every one of them, its version, its licence and the aports commit it was
    built from (where its source is), is listed in
    /usr/share/licenses/udeck-plugin/ALPINE-PACKAGES, made from the image's own
    package records when the image is built.

What each build links was read from the binaries of udeck-plugin 0.5.0: the
strings of the stripped static Linux binary, and the load commands and symbols
of the macOS one. Of the C that swift-foundation compiles into
FoundationEssentials (its _FoundationCShims), the Linux binary holds uuid.c —
its format strings are there, and UUID() calls it — which is under a licence
of its own (10), and platform_shims.c, string_shims.c and the Unicode tables
of CFUniCharBitmapData.inc.h — all 56 tables are there, byte for byte — which
are swift-foundation's, under its licence (4). swift-asn1, which
Packages/UDeckPluginFormat/Package.resolved also names, is a dependency of
swift-crypto's other products and no part of udeck-plugin.

The Apache License 2.0 is in LICENSE, beside this file.


